<title>MEXICO: Rains destroy 35,000 T grain in Mexican state.</title>
<headline>Rains destroy 35,000 T grain in Mexican state.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agrigulture Ministry said late Wednesday it will distribute 6.5 million pesos to grain farmers in the northern state of Nuevo Leon who lost a total ot 35,000 tonnes of grains because of recent heavy rains.</p>
<p>&quot;Due to the constant rains...more than 1,800 producers lost nearly 35,000 tonnes of sorghum, soy, beans and wheat,&quot; ministry official Tomas Garza Guillen told a news conference.</p>
<p>The ministry and the state government will help farmers replant damaged fields and reimburse them for lost production, Garza Guillen said.</p>
<p>((--Jacqueline Lerma, Monterrey newsroom, +528 345-7677))</p>
